#include <iostream>
#include <string>
#include <sstream>

std::string markdownToHtml(const std::string& markdown) {
    // Create a new string to hold the HTML output
    std::string html;

    // Create a new string stream to hold the markdown text
    std::stringstream markdownStream(markdown);

    // Convert the markdown text to HTML using a markdown library
    // (e.g., markdowncpp)
    markdowncpp::Markdown markdown;
    markdown.convert(markdownStream, html);

    // Return the HTML output
    return html;
}
```

This function uses a markdown library to convert the markdown text to HTML. You'll need to include a markdown library in your project, such as `markdowncpp` or `libmarkdown`.

Here's an example usage:

```cpp
int main() {
    std::string markdown = "# Hello, World!\n\nThis is a markdown text.";
    std::string html = markdownToHtml(markdown);
    std::cout << html << std::endl;
    return 0;
}
```

Note that this function assumes that the markdown text is well-formed and that the markdown library is properly configured to handle the markdown syntax.

